{
  "dom_id": "step-q109850",
  "name": "Question 10",
  "problem": "Let $B$ be a $m\\times n$ matrix. What is the image of $\\text{Col}({B}^{T})$ under the action of $B?$",
  "worked_solution": "Pre-multiplying a vector $x\\in {R}^{n}$ by $B$ gives a linear combination of the columns of $B:$\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & \u22ef & | \\\\ {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} & \u22ef & {b}_{n} \\\\ | & | & \u22ef & |\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{B}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ \u22ee \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]}_{\u23df}}_{x}={x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {b}_{1} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {b}_{2} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]+\u22ef+{x}_{n}[\\begin{aligned}| \\\\ {b}_{n} \\\\ |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image of ${R}^{n}$ under the action of $B$ must be $\\text{Col}(B),$ the column space of $B.$\n\nFurthermore, since $\\text{Null}(B)$ is mapped to the zero vector $0$ by the definition of the null subspace, the image of its orthogonal complement $\\text{Col}({B}^{T})$ must be $\\text{Col}(B).$\n\nThis can be schematically visualized, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14093810/assets/ad1557fbd48206baf7239046ada69f60d8cd9ee4916b4f8e37741903ef7d1e9b.png)",
